I’ll inspect the workspace for its task scheduling conventions, then add the Monday 09:00 UTC automation without executing the report.
The host is on BST, so a plain `09:00` cron entry would run one hour early in UTC terms. I’ll add a UTC-based report script and install an hourly cron guard that invokes it only when the UTC time is Monday 09:00; this preserves the requested schedule across daylight-saving changes and will first match on Monday, August 3, 2026.
The implementation computes both adjacent full UTC weeks, filters returned rows to each requested inclusive range, and posts only the six required fields. I’m installing the schedule now, then I’ll verify the cron entry and validate the calculation code without contacting the API.
Configured the recurring weekly orders report.

- Script: `weekly_orders_report.py`
